        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6862cb28-9b82-557d-99c3-16bc3aa54254",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Costus, Boenninghausenia, Costus barbatus\n- Plant families: Costaceae, Rutaceae\n- Places: Asia, Africa, the Americas, Bhutan, Nepal, Pakistan, Kashmir, India, Indonesia, Philippines, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, Vietnam, China, Japan\n- Concepts: genus, monotypic genus, perennial herbaceous plants, cultivated species\n\nFacts:\n- In 1753, Linnaeus described Costus as a genus in the family Costaceae.\n- Costus is a group of perennial herbaceous plants.\n- Costus is widespread through tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, Africa, and the Americas.\n- Boenninghausenia is a monotypic plant genus in the family Rutaceae.\n- Boenninghausenia albiflora is the sole species of Boenninghausenia.\n- Boenninghausenia albiflora occurs in Bhutan, Nepal, Pakistan, Kashmir, India, Indonesia, the Philippines, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, North Vietnam, China, and Japan.\n- Costus barbatus is one of the most commonly cultivated species called \"Costus\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
